      <guid isPermaLink="false">a35d7caa335fd5fcac25d9bf</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:00:06 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>In the aftermath of the global financial crisis, a Reserve Bank of India report invoked an old warning about carry trades: They were like “picking pennies off the highway” — capable of generating decent returns for years before a disastrous spell wiped out the gains. The central bank also lamented how the “carry-trade mania” had spread to Indian banks and companies borrowing abroad to make a quick buck investing in rupees.</description>
